Description: PatroneOS's name, logos and artwork
 Names the system PatroneOS and puts its logo where Ubuntu's was: the boot
 splash, the boot menu, the login screen, Settings > About, the text
 console's banner and the welcome message at login, which also loses Ubuntu's
 help links, news and Ubuntu Pro advertising. The login screen gets Patrone's
 colors and a blue default avatar. PatroneOS's fonts are the system's:
 PatroneOS Sans for the desktop, apps and the login screen, PatroneOS
 Document for documents (LibreOffice's too), PatroneOS Mono for monospace
 text, and the plain sans-serif, serif and monospace fonts for apps and web
 pages, Chromium's included. It installs the Neon Horizon
 wallpaper as the default, light in the light style and dark in the dark
 one, with variants to choose from in Settings in place of Ubuntu's
